    "created_at": "2018-01-24T19:21:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-24T19:21:50Z",
    "body": "It's not clear on the spec what should happen to the promise if we get an uncreatable ImageBitmap. That's true for `(0,0,0,0)` input as well as `(0,0,1e9,1e9)`. \r\n\r\nI think Chrome does the right thing for big numbers and the wrong thing for `0,0` size. I think ignoring the width/height (as WebKit) is weird and I have no idea what Firefox is doing, honestly. Does it fail once you try to write to the ImageBitmap? \r\n\r\nI think it's worth updating the spec to explicitly say that when the ImageBitmap can't be created because of size, the promise should fail. Or at least create compatibility bugs on the browsers to follow up on those differences.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
