    "created_at": "2018-01-26T18:23:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-26T18:31:27Z",
    "body": "Right. I think createImageBitmap should reject the promise with an exception if a resizeWidth-by-resizeHeight image cannot be allocated.  Rejecting with the promise works for cases like Blob where the cropping step is necessarily async.  It also gives implementations some latitude for performing the cropping in parallel in the cases that are not required to be executed in parallel by the spec.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
